      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: I *thought* we had a convention of assuming that `SkData` is const, so no need to mark it as such. In fact, the docs say\n\n```\n/**\n *  SkData holds an immutable data buffer. Not only is the data immutable,\n *  but the actual ptr that is returned (by data() or bytes()) is guaranteed\n *  to always be the same for the life of this instance.\n */\n```\n\nThat said I just searched for `const SkData` and have found it, sometimes like here in an `sk_sp`.\n\nAlso, admittedly, we have `writable_data`, which conflicts with that guidance.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 28,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "6170689885a06e31650a9354ee5802d073e0d5f9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
